odule task to have the command parameters on separate lines. That way, each line starts with a hyphen and is properly indented.\n\nWait, but the command module\'s \'command\' parameter is a string, so splitting it into multiple lines isn\'t straightforward. Alternatively, I can break the line by using a backslash, but that\'s not ideal. The better approach is to split the command into multiple lines by using a YAML block sequence.\n\nWait, no, the command is a single string, so I can\'t split it into multiple lines unless I use a backslash. Alternatively, I can use a multiline string by enclosing it in quotes and breaking lines with backslashes.\n\nBut in YAML, the command can be written as a single line or split into multiple lines. Let me see the exact line length.\n\nThe original command line is:\n\ncommand: dnssec-keygen -a RSASHA256 -b 2048 -s 256 -n sec -r /dev/urandom Krndc\n\nLet me count the characters. \'dnssec-keygen -a RSASHA256 -b 2048 -s 256 -n sec -r /dev/urandom Krndc\' is 64 characters. Adding \'command:\' makes it 70, which is under 80. Wait, maybe I\'m miscalculating.\n\nWait, \'command: \' is 8 characters, then the command itself is 64, totaling 72. So it\'s within the limit. Hmm, maybe I\'m looking at the wrong line.\n\nWait, perhaps the issue is elsewhere. Let me check the \'vars\' section in the \'Install the dns packages\' task. The \'vars\' are defined as:\n\nvars:\n    packages: [\'bind9\', \'bind9-utils\']\n\nThat\'s fine. Maybe the \'Create the required directories\' task:\n\n- name: Create the required directories\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    state: directory\n  loop: [\'/var/cache/bind\', \'/var/named\', \'/etc/bind.keys\']\n\nThe \'loop\' value is a list with three items, each being a string. The line \'loop: [\'/var/cache/bind\', \'/var/named\', \'/etc/bind.keys\']\' is 64 characters. \'loop:\' is 5, so total is 69, which is under 80.\n\nHmm, maybe the \'rndc key\' task\'s \'args\' section. Let me see:\n\nargs:\n    chdir: /etc/bind.keys\n\nThat\'s short. Wait, perhaps the \'Create the zone file\' task\'s \'dest\' path is too long. The \'dest\' is \'/etc/bind/zones/db.{{ zone }}\', which when \'zone\' is \'example.com\' becomes \'/etc/bind/zones/db.example.com\'. But in the playbook, it\'s written as a variable, so the line is:\n\ndest: /etc/bind/zones/db.{{ zone }}\n\nThat\'s 30 characters for the path, plus \'dest:\' makes it 36, which is fine.\n\nWait, maybe the \'Add zones to the configuration\' task\'s \'vars\' section. The \'zones\' are set to [\'127.0.0.1\'], which is 14 characters. Not an issue.\n\nWait, perhaps the \'notify\' line in the \'Place the systemd override\' task is the issue. The line is \'notify: Reload systemd daemon\', which is 30 characters. No, that\'s fine.\n\nWait, perhaps I\'m missing something. The error message says line 33, column 81. Let me count the lines in the playbook to see which task is on line 33.\n\nLooking at the playbook:\n\nLine 1: ---\nLine 2: - name: Import assert.yml and run it once on localhost\nLine 3:   include_tasks: assert.yml\nLine 4:   host: localhost\nLine 5: \nLine 6: - name: Install the dns packages\nLine 7:   apt:\nLine 8:     name: "{{ packages }}"\nLine 9:     state: present\nLine 10:   vars:\nLine 11:     packages: [\'bind9\', \'bind9-utils\']\nLine 12: \nLine 13: - name: Create the required directories\nLine 14:   file:\nLine 15:     path: "{{ item }}"\nLine 16:     state: directory\nLine 17:   loop: [\'/var/cache/bind\', \'/var/named\', \'/etc/bind.keys\']\nLine 18: \nLine 19: - name: Create the required group\nLine 20:   group:\nLine 21:     name: named\nLine 22:     state: present\nLine 23: \nLine 24: - name: Create the required user\nLine 25:   user:\nLine 26:     name: named\nLine 27:     group: named\nLine 28:     home: /var/named\nLine 29:     shell: /sbin/nologin\nLine 30:     state: present\nLine 31: \nLine 32: - name: Generate the rndc key\nLine 33:   command: dnssec-keygen -a RSASHA256 -b 2048 -s 256 -n sec -r /dev/urandom Krndc\nLine 34:   args:\nLine 35:     chdir: /etc/bind.keys\nLine 36: \nLine 37: - name: Set permissions on the rndc key file\n... and so on.\n\nAh, line 33 is the command line for generating the rndc key. The line starts with \'command: ...\' and the command itself is 64 characters, making the total line length 72, which is under 80. So why is yamllint complaining about line 33 being too long?\n\nWait, maybe I\'m miscalculating. Let me count the exact characters in line 33:\n\ncommand: dnssec-keygen -a RSASHA256 -b 2048 -s 256 -n sec -r /dev/urandom Krndc\n\nThat\'s \'command: \' (8) + \'dnssec-keygen -a RSASHA256 -b 2048 -s 256 -n sec -r /dev/urandom Krndc\' (64) = 72 characters. That\'s under 80, so why the error?\n\nWait, perhaps the error is in another line. Let me check the \'vars\' section in the \'Create the zone file\' task. The \'dest\' is \'/etc/bind/zones/db.{{ zone }}\', which when \'zone\' is \'example.com\' becomes \'/etc/bind/zones/db.example.com\'. But in the playbook, it\'s written as a variable, so the line is:\n\ndest: /etc/bind/zones/db.{{ zone }}\n\nThat\'s 30 characters for the path, plus \'dest:\' makes it 36, which is fine.\n\nWait, perhaps the \'vars\' in the \'Add zones to the configuration\' task:\n\nvars:\n    zones: [\'127.0.0.1\']\n\nThat\'s fine. Hmm, maybe I\'m looking at the wrong line. Let me check the \'notify\' line again.\n\nIn the \'Place the systemd override\' task, the line is:\n\nnotify: Reload systemd daemon\n\nThat\'s 30 characters, so no issue.\n\nWait, perhaps the error is in the \'rndc key\' task\'s \'args\' line. Let me check:\n\nargs:\n    chdir: /etc/bind.keys\n\nThat\'s short. Hmm, maybe I\'m missing something else. Let me check the \'rndc key\' task again. Oh, perhaps the \'command\' is written as a single line, but the actual command is too long. Alternatively, perhaps the line is actually longer due to the way YAML handles indentation.\n\nWait, in YAML, each line after the first in a task is indented. So,