content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s detailed instructions. Let me go through each task step by step to ensure I understand what\'s required.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the first line. That\'s straightforward. It should be a valid YAML file, conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint standards, so I need to make sure the syntax is correct.\n\nThe tasks need to be structured so they can be included directly in an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory, specifically tasks/main.yml. So, I\'ll structure each task as a list under the \'tasks\' key.\n\nLooking at Task 1, it uses the stat module to check if /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ exists. The result goes into grub_efi. I\'ll set the path and register the variable.\n\nNext, Task 2 deletes /boot/grub2/grub.cfg only if the efi directory exists. I\'ll use the file module with state=absent and conditionally only run when grub_efi is true.\n\nTask 3 copies a template to /etc/grub.d/01_users. It uses the template module, sets the correct permissions and ownership, and triggers the Update grub handler. I\'ll make sure the dest, template, and mode are correctly specified.\n\nTask 4 adds a password line to /etc/grub2-efi.cfg after the EOF marker. Using lineinfile, I\'ll set the line and ensure it\'s after the marker. This also triggers the Update handler.\n\nTask 5 is similar to Task 4 but targets /etc/grub2.cfg instead. Again, using lineinfile and the same handler.\n\nTask 6 modifies grub configuration files to add --unrestricted if the variable is true. It uses replace and targets multiple files as specified. The handler is triggered here as well.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks have the correct modules, parameters, and that variables are properly referenced. Also, each task must trigger the Update grub handler where specified.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, arguments, and any conditions using \'when\'. I\'ll ensure that the YAML is properly formatted, using the correct indentation and syntax.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure there are no unnecessary elements like hosts or vars, as the tasks should be self-contained and part of a role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Get the path to the efi variables directory\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/\n  register: grub_efi\n\n- name: Remove the grub.cfg file on EFI systems\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /boot/grub2/grub.cfg\n    state: absent\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n\n- name: Install a user template for grub\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: 01_users.j2\n    dest: /etc/grub.d/01_users\n    mode: 0755\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add password to the grub configuration on EFI systems\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2-efi.cfg\n    line: "set superusers=\'root\'; password_pbkey {{ grub_password }}"\n    insertafter: EOF\n    create: yes\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add password to the grub configuration on MBR systems\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2.cfg\n    line: "set superusers=\'root\'; password_pbkey {{ grub_password }}"\n    insertafter: EOF\n    create: yes\n  when: grub_efi.stat.exists\n  notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Modify the grub configuration to allow unrestricted access\n  ansible.builtin.replace:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    replace: " {{ grub_password_unrestricted_flag }}"\n    with: " {{ grub_password_unrestricted_flag }} --unrestricted"\n    regexp: "(^\\\\s*)"\n  when: grub_password_unrestricted\n  with_items: "{{ grub_password_unrestricted_files }}"\n  notify: Update grub\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T15:06:09.532511554Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16847550405, 'load_duration': 88282096, 'prompt_eval_count': 634, 'prompt_eval_duration': 365098629, 'eval_count': 88