content='<think>\nAlright, let\'s break down how I approached creating the Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. \n\nFirst, I read the user\'s query carefully. They wanted a Playbook that starts with \'---\', adheres to YAML and Ansible lint standards, and can be included in an Ansible Role. The Playbook must have three specific tasks in order.\n\nTask 1 is to gather bootstrap facts by executing a shell command to display /etc/os-release and store the output in a variable. I chose the shell module because it\'s straightforward for executing commands. I made sure to set \'become: false\' to prevent privilege escalation and used \'register\' to capture the output.\n\nNext, Task 2 involves setting distribution facts by iterating over a list. I used the loop with a flattened list from bootstrap_os_family_map. The \'when\' condition ensures it only runs if the previous task succeeded, the distribution variable isn\'t set, and a specific pattern in os-release matches. I extracted the distribution and major version usingansible expressions.\n\nFor Task 3, I needed to set OS family facts by looping over a dictionary. I used \'dict\' to iterate over items and set the family variable when the distribution matches an item\'s value. Again, \'become: false\' was included.\n\nI made sure each task uses the correct module and parameters, following the exact instructions without adding or omitting anything. The YAML structure was kept clean to pass linting checks.\n\nFinally, I structured the Playbook starting with \'---\' and each task in the specified order, ensuring it\'s valid and can be included in an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Gather Bootstrap Facts\n  shell: cat /etc/os-release\n  register: bootstrap_facts\n  become: false\n\n- name: Set Bootstrap Distribution Facts (I)\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap_os_family_map | flatten }}"\n  vars:\n    bootstrap_search: "{{ item }}"\n  when:\n    - previous_task_result.rc == 0\n    - not bootstrap_distribution\n    - "{{ bootstrap_facts.stdout }} | match(bootstrap_search)"\n  shell: echo "{{ bootstrap_facts.stdout | regex_replace(\'/etc/os-release\', \'\') | split(\'\\n\') | map(\'split\', \':\') | selectattr(1, \'match\', \'^\\"?([^\\"]+)\') | map(attribute=1) | list | first }}"\n  register: dist_var\n  become: false\n  vars:\n    bootstrap_distribution: "{{ dist_var.stdout | first | replace(\'"\', \'\') }}"\n    bootstrap_distribution_major_version: "{{ dist_var.stdout | last | replace(\'"\', \'\') }}"\n\n- name: Set Bootstrap OS Family Facts (II)\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap_os_family_map | dict }}"\n  vars:\n    family_search: "{{ item.value.distribution }}"\n  when: bootstrap_distribution is in (item.value.distribution)\n  shell: echo "{{ item.key }}"\n  register: family_var\n  become: false\n  vars:\n    bootstrap_os_family: "{{ family_var.stdout }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T15:16:19.809565551Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12101476973, 'load_duration': 67998850, 'prompt_eval_count': 459, 'prompt_eval_duration': 135829355, 'eval_count': 621, 'eval_duration': 11896800740, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e3378dc2-ce62-4952-87ee-a69afc889b9e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 459, 'output_tokens': 621, 'total_tokens': 1080}
