ive to the main playbook?\n- Are all necessary modules used correctly, like `apt`, `dnf`, `pacman`, `yum`, `zypper`?\n\nI should also ensure that each task is properly ordered and that the conditions are accurately reflecting the package manager detection.\n\nPutting it all together, the playbook will start by detecting the package manager, then include the appropriate tasks based on that detection. Each included task file will handle the specific configuration and updates needed for its respective package manager.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Detect package manager\n  shell: which package_manager 2>/dev/null || which apt 2>/dev/null || which dnf 2>/dev/null || which pacman 2>/dev/null || which yum 2>/dev/null || which zypper 2>/dev/null\n  register: package_manager\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Set fact for package manager\n  set_fact:\n    package_manager: "{{ package_manager.stdout }}"\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager assert\n  include_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager apk\n  include_tasks: apk.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/apk\'\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager apt\n  include_tasks: apt.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/apt\'\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager dnf\n  include_tasks: dnf.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/dnf\'\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager pacman\n  include_tasks: pacman.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/pacman\'\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager yum\n  include_tasks: yum.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/yum\'\n\n- name: Include tasks for package manager zypper\n  include_tasks: zypper.yml\n  when: package_manager.stdout == \'/usr/bin/zypper\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T15:39:15.674223123Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14672095259, 'load_duration': 100278934, 'prompt_e