mand expects the vhost name as an argument, so I\'ll pass that correctly in the command module.\n\nI should also ensure that the tasks are in the correct order: create directories first, then copy configs, then enable sites.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the entire playbook starts with \'---\' and each task is properly indented and formatted according to YAML standards. No extra comments or explanations, just the tasks as specified.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the document root directory for each vhost\n  file:\n    path: /var/www/vhosts/{{ item }}/html\n    state: directory\n    mode: 755\n  loop:\n    - "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n\n- name: Configure the Apache vhost configuration files\n  template:\n    src: vhost_conf_template\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/{{ item }}.conf\n  loop:\n    - "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n\n- name: Enable Apache vhosts on Debian systems\n  command: a2ensite {{ item }}\n  args:\n    chdir: /etc/apache2/sites-enabled\n  loop:\n    - "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T16:27:23.419047967Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12032153156, 'load_duration': 86875843, 'prompt_eval_count': 390, 'prompt_eval_duration': 82845893, 'eval_count': 690, 'eval_duration': 11861659917, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--fdc8d2a6-b06e-45b7-ad37-65a8e44a014a-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 390, 'output_tokens': 690, 'total_tokens': 1080}
