he playbook with \'---\', then define the tasks in the correct order. The first task imports assert.yml, and then the next set of tasks handle the service management based on the variable states.\n\nI should double-check each module call and variable name to match exactly what\'s provided. Making sure the file paths and module parameters are correct is crucial to avoid any errors during execution.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the entire playbook to ensure it meets all the user\'s requirements and adheres to the specified structure and standards. Once everything looks good, I\'ll present the YAML code as the final answer.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- import_tasks: assert.yml\n  no_cache: true\n\n- name: Manage automatic service management for the system\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Disable automatic service management on installation\n    file:\n      path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n      content: \'#!/bin/sh\\nexit 101\'\n      mode: 755\n    when: apt_autostart_state == "disabled"\n\n  - name: Enable automatic service management on installation\n    file:\n      path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n      state: absent\n    when: apt_autostart_state == "enabled"\n\nvars:\n  apt_autostart_state: "disabled"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T17:00:10.176121144Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12277372843, 'load_duration': 94390829, 'prompt_eval_count': 400, 'prompt_eval_duration': 93969339, 'eval_count': 708, 'eval_duration': 12088037743, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7931416e-c239-4778-955d-94f36b6e9e9c-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 400, 'output_tokens': 708, 'total_tokens': 1108}
