content='<think>\nOkay, so I need to fix the Ansible playbook that\'s failing ansible-lint. Let\'s go through each error one by one and figure out how to correct them without changing the tasks\' functionality.\n\nFirst, looking at the error messages:\n\n1. The `command` module doesn\'t accept setting environment variables inline. But in the original playbook, Task 3 uses `ansible.builtin.command`, and the error is about inline environment variables. Wait, the task doesn\'t set any inline env vars, so maybe it\'s a different issue. Oh, perhaps it\'s because the command uses `set -o pipefail`, which is a shell built-in. The `command` module runs commands without shell processing, so `set -o pipefail` might not work as expected. So maybe we should switch to the `shell` module which uses a shell.\n\n2. The next error is about the `no-changed-when` rule. It says commands should not change things if nothing needs doing. That usually happens when a command always changes something, like `echo "test" > /tmp/file`. In our case, the command in Task 3 is `php -r \'echo ini_loaded_file();\'`. If this command doesn\'t modify anything, maybe ansible-lint is flagging it. But since we\'re using `ignore_errors: true`, perhaps that\'s causing it. Alternatively, maybe the task isn\'t idempotent, but I\'m not sure.\n\n3. The third error is about the `mode: 644` being a risky octal literal. Ansible recommends using quoted strings for octal modes, like `mode: "0644"`.\n\n4. There are some warnings about other collections, but those are just warnings and not blocking.\n\nSo, to fix these:\n\n- For the first issue, change the `ansible.builtin.command` module to `ansible.builtin.shell` because we need to set `set -o pipefail` which requires a shell. This will fix the inline env var issue and the no-changed-when warning.\n\n- For the mode issue, change `mode: 644` to `mode: "0644"` to follow Ansible\'s best practices.\n\nLet me check the tasks:\n\nTask 3 uses `ansible.builtin.command`, so I\'ll switch that to `ansible.builtin.shell`. Also, in the command, we have `set -o pipefail` which is correct in shell but not in command. So changing the module should fix that.\n\nIn the `configure_php_settings` task, the mode is set to 644. I\'ll change that to "0644".\n\nI\'ll make these changes and ensure the rest of the playbook remains the same. Let me write out the corrected playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import the assert.yml file\n  ansible.builtin.import_playbook:\n    name: assert.yml\n    run_once: true\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Install the PHP packages\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ php_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Find the location of the used php.ini file\n  ansible.builtin.shell:\n    cmd: "{{ php_ini_command }}"\n    register: php_found_ini_location\n    ignore_errors: true\n\n- name: Configure the PHP settings\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: php.ini.j2\n    dest: "{{ php_ini_location | default(php_found_ini_location.stdout) }}"\n    mode: "0644"\n  notify: restart httpd\n\n- name: Ensure httpd service is restarted\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: httpd\n    state: restarted\n  listen: restart httpd\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T17:27:18.423548737Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 18679000329, 'load_duration': 85951678, 'prompt_eval_count': 1861, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1220878234, 'eval_count': 773, 'eval_duration': 17370978753, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--2a05f75b-a94a-48d5-b420-1482735e32b2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1861, 'output_tokens': 773, 'total_tokens': 2634}
