content='<think>\nOkay, so I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me go through each task and figure out how to translate them into YAML.\n\nStarting with Task 1: Create the RKE2 config directory. I know that in Ansible, the file module can create directories. So I\'ll use file state=directory, with path /etc/rancher/rke2. I should set the owner to root and group to root, maybe. Also, the mode should be 0755, I think that\'s standard for directories.\n\nTask 2 and 3 are about setting the combined_node_taints variable based on the node type. So I\'ll use the set_fact module. For Task 2, only if rke2_type is \'server\', I set combined_node_taints to rke2_server_node_taints. Similarly for Task 3, but for \'agent\' type. I need to make sure the conditions are correctly written using the ansible facts.\n\nTask 4 is about copying the RKE2 config. I\'ll use the copy module, source from the given path, destination to /etc/rancher/rke2/config.yaml. Then, set owner to rancher and group rancher, mode 0644. Also, I need to notify the Config file changed handler, which I\'ll add as a notify section.\n\nTask 5 is similar but for the kubelet config, and it\'s conditional on rke2_kubelet_config not being empty. So I\'ll use copy again, but only when that variable is not empty. The destination is /etc/rancher/rke2/kubelet.yaml. Same owner and group, and notify the handler.\n\nTask 6 is about the Containerd Registry Configuration. Again, using copy, but only if either of the two variables is not empty. Destination is /etc/containerd/config.json. Then, set owner to rancher, group rancher, and notify the handler.\n\nTask 7 is to start the RKE2 service on the rest of the nodes. I\'ll use the service module. The name is rke2-{{ rke2_type }}. I need to ensure it\'s started and enabled. Also, set to restarted, with retries and a delay. Notify the Service (re)started handler.\n\nTask 8 is to mask other RKE2 services. I\'ll iterate over services that are not of type rke2_type. So, loop through each service in rke2_other_services, and use the service module to mask them (disable and stop). Maybe the mask service name is something like rke2-{{ item.type }}.\n\nTask 9 and 10 are wait tasks. For Task 9, without CNI, I need to wait for nodes to be ready. I\'ll use the wait_for_task module, loop over each node in the group, and check if the status is ready. Retries and delay as specified.\n\nTask 10 is similar but with CNI, checking the number of ready nodes. I think it\'s about waiting for all nodes except the current one to be ready. So, the loop would iterate over the group, and for each node, check if it\'s the active server or the first in the group, then wait for the rest.\n\nI need to make sure that all tasks are in the correct order and that the YAML is valid. Also, each task should use the correct modules and variables. I should check for any typos and ensure that the YAML structure is correct, with proper indentation.\n\nWait, for the service modules in Task 7 and 8, I need to make sure the names are correctly parameterized. Also, the notify section should have the correct handler names, like Config file changed and Service (re)started.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll structure each task as per the YAML format, ensuring that all conditions and loops are correctly implemented.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the RKE2 config directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rancher/rke2\n    state: directory\n    owner: rancher\n    group: rancher\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Set server taints\n  set_fact:\n    combined_node_taints: "{{ rke2_server_node_taints }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'server\'\n\n- name: Set agent taints\n  set_fact:\n    combined_node_taints: "{{ rke2_agent_node_taints }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'agent\'\n\n- name: Copy RKE2 config\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ rke2_config_source }}"\n    dest: /etc/rancher/rke2/config.yaml\n    owner: rancher\n    group: rancher\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: Config file changed\n\n- name: Copy kubelet config\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ rke2_kubelet_config_source }}"\n    dest: /etc/rancher/rke2/kubelet.yaml\n    owner: rancher\n    group: rancher\n    mode: 0644\n  when: rke2_kubelet_config is not empty\n  notify: Config file changed\n\n- name: Copy Containerd Registry Configuration file\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ rke2_containerd_registry_config_source }}"\n    dest: /etc/containerd/config.json\n    owner: rancher\n    group: rancher\n    mode: 0644\n  when: rke2_custom_registry_mirrors is not empty or rke2_custom_registry_configs is not empty\n  notify: Config file changed\n\n- name: Start RKE2 service on the rest of the nodes\n  service:\n    name: rke2-{{ rke2_type }}\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n    restarted: true\n    delay: 5s\n    retries: 5\n  notify: Service (re)started\n\n- name: Mask other RKE2 service on the rest of the nodes\n  service:\n    name: rke2-{{ item.type }}\n    state: stopped\n    enabled: no\n  loop: "{{ rke2_other_services }}"\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI\n  wait_for_task:\n    task: >\n      set_fact:\n        node_ready: true\n      when: >\n        ({{ node.status == \'Ready\' }}\n          and ({{ node roleName == \'server\' }}\n            or ({{ node roleName == \'agent\' }}\n              and {{ nodeReady }}\n              and {{ nodeNetworkReady }})))\n    retries: 30\n    delay: 10\n    until: node_ready is true\n  loop: "{{ groups[\'rke2_nodes\'] }}"\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - with CNI\n  wait_for_task:\n    task: >\n      set_fact:\n        nodes_ready: true\n      when: >\n        ({{ansible_hostname == server_hostname }}\n          or ({{ ansible_hostname == groups[\'rke2_nodes\'][0] }}\n            and {{ groups[\'rke2_nodes\']|length > 1 }})\n          or ({{ groups[\'rke2_nodes\']|length == 1 }))\n        )\n        and ({{ total_ready_nodes >= total_nodes - 1 }})\n    retries: 30\n    delay: 10\n    until: nodes_ready is true\n```' additional_kwar