s used for executing commands.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure each task with their respective modules, arguments, and any conditions or notifications. I\'ll ensure the YAML is valid, using proper indentation and no extra comments unless necessary.\n\nWait, for the notify, I think the shell module can\'t notify handlers directly. Oh, right, I should use the \'notify\' parameter in the shell task. Alternatively, maybe I should use a separate handler. But the user specified to include exactly the tasks as described, so I\'ll proceed with the shell task having the notify.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll write the YAML, making sure each task is correctly formatted and in the right order.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Restart RKE2 service on a node\n  shell: sudo systemctl restart rke2.service\n  become: true\n  notify: Service (re)started\n\n- name: Wait for all nodes to be ready again\n  shell: kubectl get nodes -o json | jq \'.items[].status.conditions[] | select(.type=="Ready") | if .status=="True" then 1 else 0 end | add\'\n  delegate_to: "{{ ansible_hostname }}"\n  register: all_ready_nodes\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  check_mode: no\n\n- name: Wait for all pods to be ready again\n  shell: kubectl get pods -o json | jq \'.items[] | if .status.phase | contains("Running") or contains("Succeeded") then 0 else 1 end | add\'\n  delegate_to: "{{ ansible_hostname }}"\n  register: all_pods_ready\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  check_mode: no\n  when: rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T18:26:27.999197073Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14906109794, 'load_duration': 2500163489, 'prompt_eval_count': 574, 'prompt_eval_duration': 378504234, 'eval_count': 868, 'eval_duration': 12025887685, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--0e2eaee1-3db2-41da-baf5-5e370434d093-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 574, 'output_tokens': 868, 'tot